## Buena Park Lemon Law FAQs

## How Do I Know If My Vehicle Qualifies Under California Lemon Law?

Any vehicle sold with a warranty may qualify for a California lemon law claim. The warranty may change depending on the manufacturer. It typically is three years from the date of purchase or 36,000 miles. You can report the defect anytime during the warranty. The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty. It’s a misconception. But, the court may view your claim more favorably if made within the early 18-month/18,000-mile window.

## What If I File a Claim without an Attorney?

Technically, you can file the claim on your own. But, hiring a qualified lawyer has its advantages. Manufacturers often reject claims. They also have a team of lawyers who use different tactics to avoid taking responsibility for a lemon. Your lawyer knows this. They can help you seek the compensation you deserve. That’s why you need a trusted lemon law lawyer in California.

## Is There a Time Limit to File the Claim?

California lemon law gives you a four-year window to file your claim. However, we recommend filing it as soon as possible. Claims filed sooner are viewed more favorably. But more importantly, driving a defective vehicle puts you, your loved ones, and others at risk. So, do it as soon as possible.

## Can I Request a Replacement?

Yes, you can request a replacement vehicle from the manufacturer. It can be the same model or the one with the same value. The law requires the manufacturer to provide a buyback. They may replace your vehicle if agreed upon. However, we recommend getting a buyback.

## Is California Lemon Law Applicable to Private Car Sales?

Typically, private vehicle sales fall under the “as is” assumption. If you end up with a lemon, you may not have a claim, even with the help of a seasoned lemon law lawyer in California.

## How Long Will It Take to Settle a Lemon Law Case?

Most lemon law cases can be resolved in a few weeks or months. Sometimes, it can take longer. We generally try to settle these claims in 30 days. But there are no guarantees. Each case is unique, and its complexity, among other factors, may affect your timeline.
